# Progress Log

The running project stage lives in [`docs/PROGRESS.md`](docs/PROGRESS.md).

## When to read

At the start of a non-trivial task, read **Current stage** and **Next up** in `docs/PROGRESS.md` before exploring or implementing. Prefer that over re-deriving status from git alone.

## When to write

After completing a meaningful chunk of work (migration applied, feature module landed, seed shipped, env/bootstrap change, deferred decision), update `docs/PROGRESS.md`:

1. Refresh **Current stage** (table + one-line stage summary).
2. Refresh **Next up** if priorities changed.
3. Prepend a dated entry under **Log** (newest first). Record what changed, where (paths / project ref), and what was explicitly deferred.

Do not delete or rewrite older log entries. Do not edit plan files to track progress — use this log.
